# Changelog — 2026-03-05 02:03

## Ad hoc: Enable file watcher for terminal-driven file trees

### Summary
The file tree watcher was completely disabled when `isTerminalTree` was true, meaning new files created in the terminal wouldn't appear in the file tree until a tab switch or directory change. Removed the blanket skip so the watcher runs for all file tree views. Drive root protection (C:\, D:\) was already handled separately.

### Changes

| File | Change |
|------|--------|
| `src/renderer/components/FileTree.tsx` | Removed `if (isTerminalTree) return` guard from file watcher useEffect; removed `isTerminalTree` from dependency array |

### Rationale
Users expect to see new files appear in the file tree immediately after creating them in the terminal. The watcher already had safeguards against watching drive roots and system directories.

